00:44:15.200 --> 00:44:16.770
But, resting in a fetal position

00:44:16.770 --> 00:44:17.730
that's curled up too tightly

00:44:17.730 --> 00:44:19.410
can restrict breathing in your diaphragm,

00:44:19.410 --> 00:44:21.240
and it can leave you feeling
a bit sore in the morning.

00:44:21.240 --> 00:44:23.580
Particularly, if you have
arthritis in your joints or back.

00:44:23.580 --> 00:44:25.920
Which I have both of those things.

00:44:25.920 --> 00:44:29.180
Prevent these woes by
straightening out your body

00:44:29.180 --> 00:44:30.020
as much as you can

00:44:30.020 --> 00:44:31.600
instead of tucking your
chin into your chest

00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:32.840
and pulling your knees up high.

00:44:32.840 --> 00:44:34.270
You can also reduce strain on you hips

00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:36.360
by placing a pillow between your knees.

00:44:36.360 --> 00:44:41.360
And of course the most
unpopular and final position,

00:44:41.480 --> 00:44:42.450
is sleeping on your stomach.

00:44:42.450 --> 00:44:44.630
Which is what my dad does.

00:44:44.630 --> 00:44:46.400
While this good for easing snoring,

00:44:46.400 --> 00:44:48.213
it's bad for practically everything else.

00:44:48.213 --> 00:44:50.540
7% of adults pick this pose,

00:44:50.540 --> 00:44:51.990
but it can lead to back and neck pains

00:44:51.990 --> 00:44:54.440
since it's hard to keep your
spine in a neutral position.

00:44:54.440 --> 00:44:56.570
Plus stomach sleepers put pressure

00:44:56.570 --> 00:44:57.730
on their muscles and joints,

00:44:57.730 --> 00:44:59.650
possibly leading to numbness, tingling,

00:44:59.650 --> 00:45:01.330
aches and irritated nerves.

